course: dictionary
lesson: 1943
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Commit is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, just as you do with any context clue.
explain: «Offering to break into accounts for money is offering to commit a crime.» The word crime is the clue. Commit here means to do something wrong. Ask yourself: is this about doing something wrong, making a promise, or learning something?
explain: «She is committed to her football team and trains every evening.» Here commit means she has promised her time and effort. Another meaning is «commit it to memory», which means learn it by heart. Check the clue words before you choose a meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Commit a crime» means to do something illegal.
fact: «Commit to» something means to promise your time and effort to it.
fact: «Commit to memory» means to learn something by heart.
fact: On a computer, to commit changes means to save them officially, as in a program.
exercise: «Standing by laughing while someone commits a crime can still get you questioned by the police.» What does commits mean here? | To learn something by heart | *To do something illegal | To save a file on a computer | To promise to help someone
exercise: «Mia has committed herself to the school choir and goes to every practice.» What does committed suggest? | *She has promised her time and effort | She has been sent away | She has forgotten the words | She is feeling sad
exercise: Sam says, «I need to commit this poem to memory before Friday.» What does Sam need to do? | Type the poem into a computer program | Send the poem to the police | *Learn the poem by heart | Forget the poem
test: In «The judge will commit him to prison», what does commit mean? | Promise to visit him | *Send him there officially | Learn about prisons | Break into the prison
test: Ravi says, «I will commit to reading for twenty minutes every night.» What does commit to mean? | Commit a crime | Write a letter | Forget about reading | *Promise to give time and effort
exam: Which sentence uses commit to mean learn by heart? | «He committed himself to the team.» | *«Practise the times tables until you can commit them to memory.» | «The program will save the changes when you press save.» | «The thief tried to commit a crime.»
